# The probes of the first adversarial review (docs/reviews/own-1.md): one line per function.
# bad*: ownership bugs the checker used to call clean. fp*: correct programs it used to report. ctrl*: controls.
# badIteratorAfterGrow and okPutAssumeCapacity are correct and clean.
# ctrlGetPtrThenPut is correct only because a hash map's first allocation has spare slots (std's growth policy): a known false positive.
# badLinearInList is clean and counted: the footer says "1 linear values handed to memory it does not follow" (tools/run_own.sh checks it).
# badLinearBytes is unproven: a pointer to a linear value goes to a function that copies bytes.
review1.badAddManyAsSlice error
review1.badAddOne error
review1.badAtomicLoad error
review1.badAtomicRmw error
review1.badComptimeSkipConsume error
review1.badErrdeferLeak error
review1.badFieldParentPtr error
review1.badFreeSubslice error
review1.badFromOwnedSlice error
review1.badGetOrPutThenGrow error
review1.badInsert error
review1.badIteratorAfterGrow clean
review1.badKeyIteratorAfterGrow error
review1.badLabeledLeak error
review1.badLinearBytes unproven
review1.badLinearInList clean
review1.badMultiSliceAfterGrow error
review1.badRecFree error
review1.badRecPool error
review1.badTryLeak error
review1.boxList clean
review1.ctrlGetPtrThenPut error
review1.ctrlSwitchLeak error
review1.ctrlUseAfterFree error
review1.fail clean
review1.fpComptimeDeadDouble clean
review1.fpEnsureNoGrow clean
review1.fpExpandToCapacity clean
review1.fpGetOrPutAssume clean
review1.fpLockPointers clean
review1.fpPopKeepsFirst clean
review1.fpPutAfterEnsure clean
review1.fpShrinkKeepsFirst clean
review1.fpToOwnedAssert clean
review1.freeHandleRec clean
review1.freeRec clean
review1.limitRemapZero error
review1.limitResizeZero error
review1.okDeferConsume clean
review1.okIfOptional clean
review1.okPutAssumeCapacity clean
